<title>INDIA: Indian soy prices rise to record levels.</title>
<headline>Indian soy prices rise to record levels.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices touched new highs on Monday gaining by 300-400 rupees per tonne, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soybean was quoted at 12,600-12,950 per tonne in market and 12,800-13,100 rupees in plant delivery condition. Dealers said purchasing demand was good against limited arrivals.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm in limited selling from soybean processing plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent was up by 400 and soyoil refined gained by 200 rupees.</p>
<p>Dealer said soymeal prices remained at a high level while rapeseed extraction was steady at previous price levels. Soymeal yellow was $275-276 and soymeal black was $246-248 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $112-113 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,825-3,850 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 3,800-3,825 FOR Bhavnagar port.</p>
